7	 A parent subloop evaluates its seed before child creation and maps its output after observing the child's terminal sequence. A failed parent mapping keeps that completion in the event log. The parent owns the error and the child retains its actual status. When a child itself fails, the existing child link leads to its authoritative failure and any inference submission evidence.
