10	+
11	 Provider exceptions from decision evaluation use a shared fixed summary instead of raw diagnostics. The catch-all also sanitizes errors carrying `DECIDER_*`: it stores a recognized code and the selected strategy when available, without provider messages or stacks. Engine provider warnings contain only safe name, code, numeric HTTP status, and run/node/strategy identifiers. Newly recorded ordinary internal defects expose the safe `INTERNAL_ERROR` message; their raw diagnostics are in server logs correlated by run and node when available. Historical rows and events retain their earlier content.
